Forking policy (summary — see TRADEMARK.md §4 for full text):
- Contribution forks (PRs back to upstream): allowed without permission.
  Keep the cosmostrix name/branding unchanged.
- Non-contribution forks (rebrand, relaunch, derivative product): require
  owner discussion first. Must use a different name + different branding.

Binary authenticity: every genuine build embeds the provenance depth
matrix and prints `status=verified` plus a `b3:` blake3 anchor on its
`Depth-matrix:` line — verify with `cosmostrix -V`, or run the
stronger `cosmostrix sig` (five-depth report ending
`SIGNATURE: AUTHENTIC (5/5 depths verified)`; exit code 2 means the
binary was modified after compilation). Mechanism and honest limits
are documented once in docs/INNOVATIONS.md (entry 31).

